Revert the unsafe 0142 start.s instrumentation + safe secondary-only marks +
IMEM fastboot restart reason.

Regression: 0141-only boots (console visible, CPU1 timeout panic), while
0142+0143 never reaches the console (white/shim screen) even with
`sweetearlyreset=0`.  0142's SWEET_MARK/SWEET_STAGE writes were placed in
reset_vector, start_cpu and common_start, which the BOOT CPU also executes
(clobbering x10-x12 and touching the early V=P mapping); the boot path must
stay byte-identical to the CI base.

0144 (3 files):

  osfmk/arm64/start.s
    - all 0142 hunks reverted: outside `sweet_secondary_entry` this file is
      byte-identical to the CI base (post-0141) again;
    - minimal secondary-only marks inside `sweet_secondary_entry` (PSCI CPU_ON
      entry - the boot CPU never executes it):
        mark 1 / stage 0xE0  entry reached (x0 = context = logical cpu id)
        mark 0x12 / stage 0xE2  firmware entered the secondary at EL2
        mark 2 / stage 0xE3  EL1 path, just before b LowResetVectorBase
      Register safety: no stack exists at PSCI CPU_ON entry, so nothing is
      pushed via SP (stp x29,x30 is not possible); the macro uses only
      x2/x3/x16/x17 (dead at this entry - SMCCC only defines x0), never
      touches x0/x1 or x18-x30, saves x0 in x2 and restores it at every exit,
      and computes the MMU-off physical address with the existing
      PA(sym) = PC_pa + (sym_VA - entry_VA) trick.  `dsb sy` after each store.

  iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetCPU.cpp
    - unchanged (C marks 5/6/7 in initCPU and the panic/IOLog diagnostics that
      print mark/stage/vec/init/sig are kept).

  bsd/dev/onc_emmc.c
    - `sweet_early_reset_install()` (0143) additionally writes the Qualcomm
      IMEM restart reason 0x77665500 ("bootloader") at physical 0x0860065c
      before arming the safety WDT, so an early panic reset goes to FASTBOOT
      (host loop already handles that).  `sweetearlyfb=0` disables.
      onc_emmc_init() clears the reason after a live boot passes the early
      phase, so later resets (sweetrebootat) still land in TWRP;
      banner "SWEET RESET: restart reason cleared (normal boot)".

  osfmk/arm/arm_init.c
    - kprintf markers around the 0143 call in arm_init():
        "SWEET RESET: arm_init hook +" / "SWEET RESET: arm_init hook -"
      The call stays right after PE_init_cpu(), which is after arm_vm_init()
      (post-0141 arm_init.c line 544) and after PE_init_printf(FALSE) - see
      plan.

